  "worked_solution": "We model the amount of debt remaining using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}=-0.5L.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nL(t)={L}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.5t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${L}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that $$32\\,000$ were borrowed, so we have ${L}_{0}=32\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the amount of debt $L$ remaining at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nL(t)=32\\,000\\,{e}^{-0.5t}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the amount of debt remaining when $t=8,$ we substitute $t=8$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(8) & =32\\,000\\,{e}^{-0.5\\cdot 8} \\\\  & =32\\,000\\,{e}^{-4} \\\\  & \u2248586.100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that $586$ dollars of debt remain.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
